# MGIF P2 Gate Repair and Verification

Date: 2026-08-23

## Finding and repair

The first isolated Clang/Ninja preflight failed on the protected
`loader/TinyGltfImplementation.cpp` edge:

```text
compile_commands and raw Ninja arguments differ for protected edge
(WindowsPath('G:/MGIF/loader/TinyGltfImplementation.cpp'),
 'cmakefiles/scene_editor_document.dir/loader/tinygltfimplementation.cpp.obj')
```

CMake's `compile_commands.json` used Windows backslashes in the `-o` and `-c`
path arguments while Ninja 1.13.2 emitted forward slashes for the same paths.
`tools/generate_editor_dependency_identity.py` now normalizes separators only
for path-bearing compiler arguments during the cross-evidence comparison; the
compiler identity, source identity, target census, preflight ancestry, and
Ninja dependency database checks remain fail-closed and unchanged.

The P2 CPU target also directly compiles code that includes GLM and TinyGLTF.
GLM is now made available before the early core-only return, and only
`p2_projection_cpu_tests` links `glm` and `tinygltf`; the locked
`scene_editor_core` and `scene_editor_document` production source/link
contracts are unchanged.

`GltfDocument` retains the private `GltfLoader` friend because the decoder
needs a read-only typed TinyGLTF view without exposing the third-party model as
a public adapter. A focused regression loads a fixture, removes its source
file, and verifies `GltfLoader::decode` still succeeds from the in-memory
document authority. The P2 test also asserts `SceneCacheSerializer` version 13
and `SceneAssetSerializer` version 10.

